Cinephora browser E2E suite
=========================

What this is
------------
A Playwright-for-Python (headless Chromium) browser test harness that boots the
real Cinephora server and verifies the `selfhost-supabase-sri` supply-chain
guarantees that the stdlib `unittest` suite cannot observe (browser-runtime
behaviour): supabase-js is fetched same-origin with no `cdn.jsdelivr.net`
request, and a tampered vendored bundle is SRI-blocked with no CDN fallback.
Adopted in ADR-003 (Cinephora-docs/decisions.md).

This suite is SEPARATE from the unit gate. The unit gate
(`python -m unittest discover -s tests`) does NOT discover or import anything
under `tests/e2e/`, so it never needs Playwright installed.

The fixture (`conftest.py`) boots `ThreadingHTTPServer` with the real
`server.Handler` on an ephemeral `127.0.0.1` port in a daemon thread. It does
NOT call `server.main()`, `init_pool()`, or `init_db()`, so NO `DATABASE_URL`
and NO Postgres are required.

Install (one-time)
------------------
From the Cinephora repo root:

    pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt
    playwright install chromium

`playwright install chromium` downloads the Chromium browser binary that the
pinned `playwright` driver drives. The `requirements-dev.txt` deps are
dev/test-only and are never imported by `server.py`.

Run
---
From the Cinephora repo root:

    pytest tests/e2e/

Headless Chromium is the pytest-playwright default; no extra flag is needed. A
failing browser-runtime security assertion fails the suite with a non-zero exit
code (no silent skips).

To keep a Playwright trace for any failing case (useful for debugging):

    pytest tests/e2e/ --tracing=retain-on-failure

CI
--
`.github/workflows/e2e.yml` runs this suite in its own optional job on push and
pull_request, installing the deps and Chromium (`playwright install --with-deps
chromium`). It is independent of the unit gate.
